.TH SHEDMAN 1 "2026-04-25" "ShedOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shedman \- unified ShedOS utility CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shedman
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B shedman
.B help
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B shedman
.B version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shedman
is a Git-style dispatcher for every utility shipped by ShedOS. It
discovers subcommands at runtime by globbing
.IR /usr/libexec/shedman/* :
each executable file in that directory is exposed as
.B shedman <name>.
Files prefixed with
.RB \(oq _ \(cq
are internal helpers, hidden from
.B shedman help
but still reachable.
.PP
The dispatcher itself only does argv preservation, name resolution,
and \(oqdid you mean\(cq suggestions on unknown commands. All
substantive logic lives in the per-subcommand binaries.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
The headline set:
.TP
.B shedman update
Interactive system upgrade (pacman + yay + config sync), bracketed
by a snapper pre/post snapshot pair. See
.BR shedman-update (1).
.TP
.B shedman apply
Reconcile
.I /etc/shedos/system.toml
against live state. See
.BR shedman-apply (1).
.TP
.B shedman doctor
Detect drift between
.I /etc/shedos/system.toml
and live state. Read-only. See
.BR shedman-doctor (1).
.TP
.B shedman rollback
Restore the root subvolume from a snapper snapshot. See
.BR shedman-rollback (1).
.TP
.B shedman config
Synchronise dotfiles and review merge conflicts. See
.BR shedman-config (1).
.TP
.B shedman status
Aggregated dashboard across the four waybar signals (updates,
conflicts, health, doctor). See
.BR shedman-status (1).
.TP
.B shedman updates / conflicts / health
The waybar-backed signal binaries. Each prints a JSON payload with
.B --waybar
and a human-readable summary by default.
.TP
.B shedman logs
Textual journalctl browser TUI.
.TP
.B shedman install
First-boot proprietary apps installer.
.TP
.B shedman migrate
One-shot retrofit for installs dated before the April 2026
packaging cut-over. Idempotent — runs on a packaged install are a
fast no-op.
.SH BUILT-INS
.TP
.B shedman
.RB \(oq help \(cq " | " --help " | " -h
List installed subcommands with one-line summaries.
.TP
.B shedman help <cmd>
Forward to
.B shedman <cmd> --help.
.TP
.B shedman version
Print the installed
.I shedos-system
version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/shedos/system.toml
Declarative source of truth (applied via
.B shedman apply
).
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/shedman/
Subcommand binaries (Git-style discovery).
.TP
.I /usr/bin/shedos-*
Silent back-compat shims for legacy
.I shedos-*
names.
.TP
.I /var/lib/shedos/
Per-section last-applied + baseline state files.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Many subcommands honour environment variables for testing — see the
per-command man pages.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shedman-update (1),
.BR shedman-apply (1),
.BR shedman-doctor (1),
.BR shedman-rollback (1),
.BR shedman-config (1),
.BR shedman-status (1),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR yay (8).
.PP
The web reference at
.UR https://shedos.org/docs/commands
.UE
covers every subcommand and flag with examples.
